--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -11,3 +11,9 @@ Every task has an `id`, a string unique within its list. It is set when the task
 when the task is renamed, so the app can keep referring to a task by its id. The methods that take a task's
 title also accept its id; the id is looked up first, so a title that happens to equal another task's id
 refers to that task.
+
+Every task also has a `createdAt`, the time it was added, and an `updatedAt`, the time it last changed. Both
+are ISO-8601 date-time strings, and they are equal until the task's first change. Completing, reopening,
+renaming, tagging or untagging a task sets `updatedAt`; a change that does nothing (renaming a task to the
+title it already has, or tagging it with a tag it already has) leaves it alone. `createTodoList` stamps
+tasks with the system clock, and takes a `now` option to read the time from elsewhere, for example in tests.
